<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/656">656</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Peada of Mercia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peada was a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a>, made ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-angles">Middle Angles</a> around 653. To marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alhflaed">Alhflæd</a>, daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu of Northumbria</a>, he accepted baptism and brought four priests to preach among his people. After Penda's death in 655 Oswiu let him rule the southern Mercians, but he was murdered in 656.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peada.jpg" alt="Peada" width="320" height="534" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tanya Dedyukhina · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peada_at_Leachfield_Cathedral_-_panoramio_(1)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
